WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.990
Obstruction is very quickly becoming the name
of the game because Donald Trump is now officially

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:06.990
retired

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:10.150
using to cooperate with the house's impeachment
inquiry.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.269
We will talk about what this means.

00:00:12.269 --> 00:00:15.940
We will talk about what will happen next,
which is really the most important question.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:23.109
I told you before that there are just too
many differences between bill Clinton's impeachment

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:28.850
and Donald Trump's impeachment to really draw
relevant parallels in terms of the course

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.820
that they might take, the outcome that they
might have.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.170
A bill Clinton's impeachment was overlying
about an affair.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.980
Donald Trump's is over borderline treasonous
behavior.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.720
Clinton wasn't tweeting all day about it.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:48.090
Donald Trump is, Clinton didn't have something
equivalent to Fox news and right wing radio

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.790
and the social media echo chambers that Donald
Trump has.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:57.530
Clinton cooperated with the inquiry while
Trump was always likely not to, and now we

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:58.730
know that he will not.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:04.699
The white house said yesterday it will not
cooperate with this impeachment inquiry period.

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:09.250
They said this in a letter of eight or nine
pages of length where he calls the entire

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:16.729
thing unconstitutional despite of course impeachment
being enshrined in the founding documents.

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:18.439
Of the United States of America.

00:01:18.439 --> 00:01:24.860
Uh, the letter is filled with complete non
arguments about why he will not be participating

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:30.299
and this is now going to set up a major battle
with Democrats in the house.

00:01:30.299 --> 00:01:35.759
This is like telling the police, no, you are
not allowed to investigate me.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:37.710
I don't participate.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:43.170
And I think you investigating my possible
crimes is harassment at the highest level.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:49.310
If you did that, the police through the courts
would enforce their right to investigate.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:54.829
And the question now is, will the house in
force, it's right to investigate, but it's

00:01:54.829 --> 00:02:01.460
actually more simply will they, will the subpoenas
even start if the subpoenas start, will the

00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.500
subpoenas be enforced?

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.110
Because you can subpoena anybody you want.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:12.480
And a court can even say, you must abide by
the subpoena, Mr. Trump, mr Trump's lawyer,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.480
whoever.

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.570
But what if you just ignore that court decision?

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.980
What if you ignore that court's decree?

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:23.180
So far there have been no consequences to
Donald Trump or others that he's directed

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:26.040
to ignore requests and subpoenas.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.850
And unless that changes, Trump's going to
get away with this.

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:34.890
This is actually, you know we, we were told
about there could be a constitutional crisis.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:37.130
This is actually a constitutional crisis.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.720
You need to understand that it's not a hypothetical
one.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:45.200
It is one right now there is no legal basis
for Donald Trump's position that a coequal

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.640
branch of government using its investigative
power is unconstitutional.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:56.600
There is no legal basis for ignoring requests
from such a constitutional inquiry.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:02.860
You can make the argument that Trump not cooperating
in and of itself is actually an impeachable

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:03.860
act.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:09.450
You could make the argument that the specifics
of the Ukraine fiasco that are being adjudicated

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:15.440
presumably by the impeachment inquiry becomes
secondary to what is clearly the impeachable

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:24.600
action of not cooperating with a legal constitutional
inquiry conducted by the power vested in a

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.530
coequal branch of government.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.630
And do you know why Trump and his lawyers
are doing this?

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:33.310
I mean you need only look at the last two
and a half years.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:39.820
It's worked so far, they suspect, and they're
not crazy to suspect it, that based on how

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:46.900
things have gone the last two years, that
ultimately they will not be forced to participate

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:52.930
or to face consequences rather if they are
told to participate but decided not to anyway.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:54.680
So why not try this?

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:59.390
My my senses and in reading a lot of legal
opinion about this over the last couple of

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:04.500
days, my sense is that even if Trump doesn't
get the gravity of the situation that he's

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.910
facing here, that his attorneys do get it.

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:13.170
And so they have made a strategic decision
that Hey, just not going along with this stuff

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.930
has served us pretty well.

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:19.360
We got Trump out of having to meet with Mueller
in person and instead he answered questions

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.360
in writing.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.360
Bogus answers.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.130
I mean deceptive answers, incomplete answers,
answers that by any normal assessment we would

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.810
say are untruths in many ways.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.470
And he got away with it.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:35.080
So this is obviously the right decision that
one would make if so far they've gotten away

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:39.340
with just not participate in getting in the
way, not doing the thing.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.980
So we've got a constitutional crisis here.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:48.370
We will soon see whether it will be resolved
in accordance with the constitution and we

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:49.370
will.

00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:53.560
I mean, listen, the most important thing at
this point is going to be are Democrats going

00:04:53.560 --> 00:05:00.840
to get it together and do everything that
they can to force compliance with this investigation?

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:02.900
Trump may still ignore it.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:08.470
Trump may still not participate, but Democrats
need to start using their subpoena power.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:12.120
They need to start looking at holding people
in contempt.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.870
There is a mechanism for doing this.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.430
We've not even really discussed it because
it seems so remote.

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:22.370
The idea is so remote to me that we would
actually see contempt.

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.840
People held in contempt by their refusal to
participate, but this is the conversation

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:27.840
we're having.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:32.480
It is a constitutional crisis right now, not
at some point in the future.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:37.740
Let me know on Twitter or in the YouTube comments,
please tell me what you think the end result

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.372
will be of Donald Trump saying we are simply
not going to participate

